'''Donna Lewis''' is a Welsh singer from [[Cardiff]], [[Wales]]. She is best known for the 1996 [[Pop music|pop]] hit single "[[I Love You Always Forever]]". Lewis teamed up with [[Richard Marx]] on the 1997 [[Adult Contemporary (chart)|adult contemporary]] hit "[[At the Beginning]]" for the ''[[Anastasia (1997 film)|Anastasia]]'' [[Anastasia (soundtrack)|soundtrack]]. In 1997, Lewis was nominated for the [[Brit Award]] for [[Brit Award for British Female Solo Artist|Best British Female Artist]].<ref name="BRITS">[http://www.brits.co.uk/artist/donna-lewis Donna Lewis BRITS Profile] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130216064849/http://www.brits.co.uk/artist/donna-lewis |date=16 February 2013 }}. BRIT Awards Ltd. Retrieved 26 January 2013</ref>

After releasing her second studio album, ''[[Blue Planet (Donna Lewis album)|Blue Planet]]'' (1998), Lewis left [[Atlantic Records]] and independently released albums ''[[Be Still (Donna Lewis album)|Be Still]]'' (2002) and ''[[In the Pink (Donna Lewis album)|In the Pink]]'' (2008). Her album ''Brand New Day'' was produced by [[David Torn]] and featured [[Ethan Iverson]], [[Reid Anderson]] and [[David King (drummer)|Dave King]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.classicalite.com/articles/13552/20141219/donna-lewis-new-album-brand-new-day-palmetto-records-david-king-reid-anderson-ethan-iverson-david-bowie-neil-young-damien-rice-burt-bacharach-gnarls-barkley-chocolate-genius-harry-nilsson.htm |title=Donna Lewis to Release New Album 'Brand New Day' Featuring David King, Reid Anderson and Ethan Iverson With Covers of David Bowie, Neil Young, Damien Rice and More |publisher=Classicalite |date=19 December 2014 |access-date=18 April 2015 |author=Prisco, Jaime}}</ref><ref name="Jazz">{{cite web |url=https://www.allaboutjazz.com/donna-lewis-brand-new-day-donna-lewis-by-ben-scholz.php?page=1 |title=Donna Lewis: Brand New Day |publisher=All About Jazz |date=10 March 2015 |access-date=4 August 2016 |author=Scholz, Ben}}</ref><ref name="Scholz">{{cite web |url=http://benjaminscholz.com/blog/26-donna-lewis-brand-new-day.html |title=Donna Lewis: Brand New Day |publisher=Benjamin Scholz |date=23 February 2015 |access-date=4 August 2016}}</ref>
